.TH BOOTSTASH 8 "September 2026" "bootstash" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
bootstash \- operator tools for bootstashd
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B bootstash
\fBcheck-config\fR
[\fB\-defaults\fR \fIpath\fR]
[\fB\-config\fR \fIpath\fR]
[\fB\-secrets\fR \fIpath\fR]
.PP
.B bootstash
\fBprovision-google\fR
[\fIoptions\fR]
.PP
.B bootstash
[\fB\-\-version\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B bootstash
is the operator CLI for the bootstash daemon. It does not serve HTTP or
call PAM.
.B provision-google
writes Google OIDC client keys into
.IR /etc/bootstash/oidc-google ;
it does not create the Google OAuth web client and it does not edit
.IR /etc/default/bootstash .
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B check-config
Parse packaged defaults,
.IR /etc/default/bootstash ,
.IR /etc/bootstash/oidc-google ,
every
.B BIND
spec, and TLS files when set. Exit 0 if the daemon could start (missing
interfaces are not an error here). Same as
.B bootstashd \-t .
.TP
.B provision-google
Print the redirect URI and Google Auth Platform URLs, then write the
Client ID and Client secret you paste to
.IR /etc/bootstash/oidc-google .
Reads
.B PUBLIC_ORIGIN
from
.I /etc/default/bootstash
(or
.BR \-origin ).
It does not create the Google OAuth web client.
.TP
.B version
Print the version from
.B git describe
(\fB\-\-version\fR,
.BR \-version ,
.B \-V
are aliases).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-config " path"
Operator config to read. Default:
.IR /etc/default/bootstash .
.TP
.BI \-secrets " path"
OIDC client secrets file. Default:
.IR /etc/bootstash/oidc-google .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR bootstashd (8),
.BR bootstash (5)
